{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/866010-am-i-alone-in-this","id":866010,"title":"Am I Alone In This?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-15T10:49:42-07:00","id":866010,"title":"Am I Alone In This?","content":"Recently picked up Beast, and despite being a little shaky on the pitch when I first heard it, I'm absolutely loving the game's premise...<br /> <br /> But, here's a thing that really strikes me, and I wonder if I'm alone in this:<br /> <br /> Does anyone else feel like, far more than even <i>Lost </i>(my favorite Co'D game ever), Beast seems like the Co'D reimagining of <i>Dreaming</i>?<br /> <br /> Mythic themes, &quot;kin&quot; ('Prodigals&quot; by any other name), the comparisons of Beasts to True Fae (and thus making Changelings literally Changelings, right out of folklore.. or Dark Ages: Fae, or the Kithain/Tuatha..), the Beast merits letting them push standard capabilities beyond mortal or usual supernatural means? Especially when you factor how rough 2E Lost are in their feeding?<br /> <br /> I know Matt's a big Dreaming fan (I've followed his blogs and websites since the Geocities days of BlackHatMatt).. was all the lovely symmetry intentional, I wonder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11533-bluegrass-beast","name":"Bluegrass Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T10:56:47-07:00","id":866013,"title":"","content":"Not particularly, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}